<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Treaty of Paris (1763)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1763</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as 1763 Treaty of Paris · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Treaty of Paris of 1763 ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seven-years-war">Seven Years' War</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> and their allies. France ceded <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a> and its territory east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mississippi-river">Mississippi</a> to Britain and lost most of its position in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/british-empire">British Empire</a> profile treats it as a foundation of British global supremacy, while the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/french-colonial-empire">French Empire</a> profile marks it as the collapse of France's first colonial empire in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-america">North America</a>.</p></div>
